{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>And Yitzchak his father answered.</b> Meaning, he gave a reason why he turned back to bless him — because of a father's compassion, for when he wept, his compassion was stirred." "<b>Behold, of the fatness.</b> Meaning, he has only what is before him, not like Jacob of whom he said ״וְיִתֶּן־לְךָ״ with the added vav — meaning, besides the eternal world, as we have explained."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:59.679783036Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}